---
import DetailHeading from '../detailHeading.astro';
---
<div class="space-y-6 text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
  <section>
    <DetailHeading>Implementation</DetailHeading>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li><span class="font-bold text-slate-300">Monorepo:</span> the public repository contains the server API and the client interface in separate application areas.</li>
      <li><span class="font-bold text-slate-300">Backend:</span> Java and Spring Boot expose the application API; PostgreSQL stores accounts and library data, while Redis supports short-lived cached data.</li>
      <li><span class="font-bold text-slate-300">Frontend:</span> React renders the library and Kanban-style progress board.</li>
      <li><span class="font-bold text-slate-300">Packaging:</span> Docker and Docker Compose describe the local application stack.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <DetailHeading>Product surface</DetailHeading>
    <p class="mt-4">
      The product supports game library organization, progress tracking, playtime, ratings, wishlist management, game search and friend requests. The final live demo is available at <a class="text-green-400 hover:underline" href="https://gameloggd.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">gameloggd.vercel.app</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <DetailHeading>Evidence boundary</DetailHeading>
    <p class="mt-4">
      The public monorepo records 37 commits. It and the live demo establish the feature scope, but do not provide public usage, latency or retention measurements.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
